# Contesting Learning Theory: A Response to Entwistle and Ekeblad.

**Authors:** Webb, Graham

## Abstract
Responds to criticisms of a paper rejecting phenomenography and the notion of &quot;deep&quot; and &quot;surface&quot; learning, noting that important arguments were not addressed, including the nature of the research relationship in phenomenography, the ahistorical stance of phenomenographers, their lack of appreciation for social/historical/power factors in determining &quot;correct&quot; conceptions, and problems in the deep/surface binary. (MSE)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ547709

